    "field": "Extreme event attribution",
    "problem": "Quantifying the likelihood of recent record warmth is challenging because past methods struggle to properly separate natural climate variability from the human-caused warming trend in serially correlated temperature data, leading to biased estimates of probability.",
    "method": "The paper proposes a semi-empirical method that combines climate model simulations with observational data to isolate and statistically model internal climate variability, which is then used to assess the likelihood of recent record warmth through Monte Carlo simulations under scenarios with and without anthropogenic forcing.",
    "task": "The task is to quantify the likelihood that recent record warm years and runs of record-setting temperatures would have occurred with and without human-caused climate change, using a semi-empirical approach that combines climate model simulations with observational data.",
